[00:14.00] All that I possess is my existence, vagrant more or less
[00:18.45] 
[00:21.16] Children on the pave, mither bad, but help me through my day
[00:27.91] This borrowed cigarette, for which my heart will leap and it will laugh
[00:34.97] A debt to you my friend, I owe but I'm afraid I cant repay
[00:40.63] BECAUSE I'M JOE, THE STREET LAMP IS MY HOME
[00:44.38] FROM PLACE TO PLACE I LIKE TO ROAM
[00:46.11] THE COLD WIND BLOWS RIGHT THROUGH MY BONES
[00:48.14] THE COLD WIND BLOWS RIGHT THROUGH MY BONES
[00:51.22] 
[01:13.23] My barrow I gave away, 'cause the muscle which pulled grew weaker every day
[01:17.29] 
[01:20.02] This soldier crossed the sea, but now the maker wages war on me
[01:27.06] This heart is still so proud, of all the things the soldier once achieved
[01:33.86] But when you're vagrant, man, no-one wants to know about such things
